# --- Enterprise gate scripts: pin line endings so CI can never fail on them ---
#
# Why this exists:
#   gate-manifest.json records each gate/machinery script's sha256. Those hashes
#   are computed over CRLF line endings, and the manifest is locked to the
#   upstream release (the manifest-provenance gate verifies it, so we cannot
#   change the hashes here). Git's default behavior checks these files out as LF
#   on Linux CI, so the skill-gate-parity gate hashes different bytes and fails.
#
# The structural fix:
#   Force every gate script to CRLF on checkout on EVERY platform and regardless
#   of any developer's core.autocrlf setting. `eol=crlf` overrides autocrlf, so
#   the bytes CI hashes are always the bytes the manifest recorded. A new gate
#   script dropped into scripts/ci is covered automatically by the glob, so this
#   cannot regress when gates are added.
scripts/ci/*.mjs text eol=crlf
scripts/ci/*.cjs text eol=crlf
scripts/ci/*.js  text eol=crlf

# Everything else: let git pick sensible line endings; never corrupt binaries.
* text=auto
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
